<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Ramdurg State</h1><p class="st-meta">1799 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Ramdurg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Maratha Brahmin state in the southern Maratha country, ruled by a branch of the family of Nargund.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Ramdurg and Nargund were held by the Bhave family, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> officials of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwas</a>. Around 1799 the holding was divided, and Ramdurg became a separate state under a branch of the family.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Under British rule Ramdurg was a minor state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-maratha-country">Southern Maratha Country</a>, later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-states-agency">Deccan States Agency</a>. Its population was mainly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannada">Kannada</a>-speaking farmers. In 1939 peasant agitation for responsible government ended in violence and police firing.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After accession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> Ramdurg was merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bombay-state">Bombay State</a> in 1948, and since 1956 its lands have been in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belagavi">Belagavi</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ramdurg-state.jpg" alt="Ramdurg State" width="320" height="321"><figcaption>Image: Germenfer · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Princely_State_of_Ramdurg.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1799 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ramdurg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kannada, Marathi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ramdurg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1874&amp;focus=ramdurg-state" aria-label="Ramdurg State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6733 1585 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ramdurg State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7053 1841L7364 1601M7053 1841L7364 1602M7053 1841L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7053 1841h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7053 1841h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1874&amp;focus=ramdurg-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
